FORMAT 1
SCENARIO Cookbook on GitHub
LABEL    Worksheet 3
SUMMARY  An empty repository on GitHub, git push, an edit on the web and git pull.
INTRO    The cookbook has five commits. On GitHub you are signed in as **jana-novakova**. The **GitHub** tab at the top is the browser.

SETUP
  PERSON jana NAME "Jana Nováková" EMAIL "novakovaj@jirovcovka.net" LOGIN "jana-novakova" LABEL "Jana's computer"
  MACHINE jana CONFIGURED
  SHOW GITHUB
  REPOSITORY git/cookbook
  PS> mkdir git
  PS> cd git
  PS> mkdir cookbook
  PS> cd cookbook
  PS> git init
  FILE pancakes.md
    # Pancakes

    ## Ingredients

    - 250 ml milk
    - 1 egg
    - 120 g plain flour
    - a pinch of salt
  END
  PS> git add .
  PS> git commit -m "Add pancake recipe"
  FILE pancakes.md
    # Pancakes

    ## Ingredients

    - 250 ml milk
    - 1 egg
    - 120 g plain flour
    - a pinch of salt

    ## Tip

    I fill them with strawberry jam.
  END
  PS> git commit -am "Add filling tip"
  FILE drop-scones.md
    # Drop scones

    ## Ingredients

    - 300 ml milk
    - 2 eggs
    - 250 g self-raising flour
    - 1 teaspoon baking powder

    ## Method

    1. Mix the ingredients.
    2. Fry small rounds in a pan.

    *Best eaten warm.*
  END
  PS> git add .
  PS> git commit -m "Add drop scones"
  FILE README.md
    # My cookbook

    Recipes I can cook.

    - [Pancakes](pancakes.md)
    - [Drop scones](drop-scones.md)
  END
  PS> git add .
  PS> git commit -m "Add cookbook contents"
  FILE .gitignore
    notes-for-me.md
  END
  PS> git add .
  PS> git commit -m "Add .gitignore"
  VSCODE git/cookbook
END

TASK On GitHub, create a repository **cookbook**: **Private** and **tick nothing**.
  NOTE     **GitHub** tab → **New** button → name `cookbook` → Private → Create repository.
  QUESTION Why do we not tick Add a README file this time?
  CHECK    github jana-novakova/cookbook exists
END

TASK Link the repository to GitHub and send it there. When signing in, choose **Sign in with your browser**.
  HINT  git remote add origin https://github.com/jana-novakova/cookbook.git
  HINT  git branch -M main
  HINT  git push -u origin main
  CHECK github jana-novakova/cookbook has branch main
END

TASK On GitHub, open **pancakes.md**, click the pencil and add a table at the end. Confirm with **Commit changes**.
  HINT  ## Servings
  HINT
  HINT  | Servings | Milk   | Flour |
  HINT  |----------|--------|-------|
  HINT  | 2        | 250 ml | 120 g |
  HINT  | 4        | 500 ml | 240 g |
  CHECK file pancakes.md on github jana-novakova/cookbook contains "|"
END

TASK Go back to VS Code and type `git status`. Then download the change.
  HINT     git status
  HINT     git pull
  QUESTION Does Git on your computer know about the change on GitHub? Why?
  CHECK    command "git pull..." was run
  CHECK    file pancakes.md contains "|"
END

TASK Add a tip to **drop-scones.md**, commit it and send it to GitHub.
  HINT  git add .
  HINT  git commit -m "Add drop scones tip"
  HINT  git push
  CHECK github jana-novakova/cookbook main equals HEAD
  CHECK commit count is at least 7
END
